# NOTE: this file is for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT of this repo only.
#
# The published server does NOT read a .env from the current directory - an MCP
# server is spawned wherever the client happens to be, so a CWD-relative file
# either picks up an unrelated project's keys or misses yours entirely.
#
# To configure the server as a user, run:      fortyguard-mcp --set-key
# To see every path it checks, run:            fortyguard-mcp --where
#
# To make THIS file take effect, point at it explicitly:
#     FORTYGUARD_ENV_FILE=/absolute/path/to/this/.env

FORTYGUARD_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# FORTYGUARD_BASE_URL=https://api.fortyguard.com

# Where paid results are archived. Defaults to the platform data directory -
# deliberately NOT a cache directory, which the OS reclaims under disk pressure.
# FORTYGUARD_DATA_DIR=

# Diagnostics, written to STDERR as JSON lines with the API key and any signed
# URLs redacted. Never stdout: under stdio that is the JSON-RPC channel.
# FORTYGUARD_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Above this many tokens, format="auto" returns a summary naming every way to
# fetch the rest. Naming a format overrides it.
# FORTYGUARD_INLINE_TOKEN_BUDGET=25000

# Optional archive cap for CI/containers. Off by default: results cost credits
# and evicting them costs credits to restore.
# FORTYGUARD_MAX_STORAGE_BYTES=
